Subject: SurfaceFlinger: free the client target's buffers when nothing is composed into them

FramebufferSurface keeps the client target's buffers (two, each the size of the display) for as
long as SurfaceFlinger runs, once it has composed into them once. A desktop display is large
(2880x2880 makes them 63 MiB), and DSA's hardware composer composes every layer on the host
except the ones it cannot (a video's YUV pictures), so the buffers sit unused most of the time.

When a frame composes nothing into the client target and the last one that did is a second old,
FramebufferSurface gives its current buffer back once that frame is presented and discards
every free buffer in its queue (the producer side forgets them through onBuffersDiscarded).
RenderSurface then drops the textures it kept for them. The next frame with client composition
dequeues, and so allocates, new buffers and sends them to HWC whole. Screenshots and screen
capture render into buffers of their own and are not affected.

Applies to frameworks/native at ae266dcb706d083868578cfedce381ef44488a07 (Android 17).
---
diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/include/compositionengine/DisplaySurface.h b/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/include/compositionengine/DisplaySurface.h
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/include/compositionengine/DisplaySurface.h
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/include/compositionengine/DisplaySurface.h
@@ -81,6 +81,11 @@
 
     // Returns true if the render surface supports client composition prediction.
     virtual bool supportsCompositionStrategyPrediction() const;
+
+    // Returns true once after the surface gave its buffers back to be freed, which it does
+    // when nothing has been composed into them for a while. Whoever keeps textures of those
+    // buffers lets go of them too, so that their memory goes.
+    virtual bool takeBuffersReleased() { return false; }
 };
 
 } // namespace compositionengine
diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/RenderSurface.cpp b/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/RenderSurface.cpp
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/RenderSurface.cpp
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/RenderSurface.cpp
@@ -249,6 +249,11 @@
 
 void RenderSurface::onPresentDisplayCompleted() {
     mDisplaySurface->onFrameCommitted();
+    if (mDisplaySurface->takeBuffersReleased() && mTexture == nullptr) {
+        // The surface discarded its buffers; the textures kept for them are the last holders.
+        // The next client composition dequeues new buffers and makes new textures.
+        mTextureCache.clear();
+    }
 }
 
